-- Generated by tools/build_manual.py; edit docs/manual/book.json.
return [====[o Magic cost</td></tr></table><p>Equip this Rare-or-better ring in either hand and stand still on solid ground for two continuous seconds. You become stone: enemies stop seeing and targeting you, and direct hits, explosions, hazards and damaging statuses cannot take your HP while Statue remains active.</p><p>Movement immediately ends Statue, including jumps, crouching, forced propulsion, moving supports and teleportation. Attacking, casting Magic, using an item or interacting also ends it, even if the action fails. Dealing HP damage ends it too. You must stand still for another full two seconds; looking around alone is allowed.</p><p>Statue costs no Magic and has no fixed duration or cooldown. It does not cure existing conditions or stop the dungeon collapse clock. Removing or moving the ring, dying, changing role or changing dungeon cancels it. An interrupted connection cannot retain an old activation.</p><p>Other players can see your stone body. A brief original transformation chime and stone flourish mark activation, and STATUE appears above your status portrait. Separate sources of invisibility retain their own rules.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 39</div></article><article class="page" id="death" data-title="Down, but not finished"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Down, but not finished</h2><div role="img" aria-label="Deborah demonstrates" class="art" style="background-size:300% 200%;background-position:50% 100%"></div><p>Heroes start with three lives. On death, your weapons, magazines, reserve ammunition, equipped wearables, stored gear, and throwable potions stay with your Hero for the respawn. Your character identity, XP, class, feats, and persistent DFT collection remain too. Reconnecting does not restore a lost life or reroll your character.</p><p>A normal death has a mandatory 20-second respawn lockout. Play Tetris while waiting, or spectate. After the lockout, press F to finalize your reward and respawn. You can keep playing until the normal 60-second death-Tetris maximum, when respawn happens automatically.</p><p>At zero lives, press F3 for three choices: wait for resurrection, begin a new Level-1 Hero, or join the Soldiers. Beginning again discards that character&#x27;s carried gear and progression but preserves account $DEB and DFTs. All Heroes may be eliminated without resetting the dungeon; only the collapse timer ends a failed run. Someone must still reach the rescue objective to clear it.</p><p>Successful rescue can bring eliminated teammates back under the campaign&#x27;s comeback rules, up to the maximum of four lives. A revived Hero returns with the same saved weapons, ammunition, wearables, stored gear, and throwable potions.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 40</div></article><article class="page" id="tetris" data-title="Make room for a comeback"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Make room for a comeback</h2><table><tr><td>One line</td><td>+10 temporary HP</td></tr><tr><td>Two lines at once</td><td>+30 temporary HP</td></tr><tr><td>Three lines at once</td><td>+50 temporary HP</td></tr><tr><td>Four lines at once</td><td>+80 temporary HP</td></tr></table><p>Move pieces left or right, rotate with Up/Forward, soft-drop with Down/Back, and hard-drop with Jump. Clearing several lines at once earns the corresponding reward, not the sum of separate single-line clears.</p><p>Rewards become temporary HP overfill. They do not permanently increase maximum HP and cannot be refilled by ordinary regeneration. Topping out ends the board session while preserving the bonus already earned; it does not erase the mandatory death wait.</p><p>After rescue, Victory Tetris lasts 20 seconds. Russian Asset doubles qualifying HP rewards in both Tetris modes. It also raises the death-Tetris maximum to 120 seconds, but F still becomes available after the same 20-second lockout. It never extends Victory Tetris or the active dungeon clock.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 41</div></article><article class="page" id="soldiers" data-title="Friends—and human foes"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Friends—and human foes</h2><p>Up to four players take cooperative Hero roles. Up to six additional players can control enemy Soldiers, for ten active players; further arrivals spectate. Role availability and the Soldier queue determine when an incarnation can be entered.</p><p>A human Soldier receives a generated monster character, class, abilities, and automatically selected feats. The player does not draft Hero feats. A fresh incarnation is a fresh Soldier character, not the revival of the previous build.</p><p>Human Soldiers can earn incarnation-local XP and automatic Combat Levels, capped by Dungeon Level +3. AI Soldiers do not earn XP. Monster-side Levels can reach 999. Soldier play preserves your eliminated Hero; return to the Hero Queue to become eligible for resurrection.</p><p>The Debbie Fund can reward Soldier-attributable Hero life losses after a successful rescue. Switching into Soldier play forfeits that player&#x27;s Hero share for that dungeon. The fund does not award a rescue pool for a timeout.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 42</div></article><article class="page" id="enemy-basics" data-title="Meet the prison staff"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Meet the prison staff</h2><p>An enemy&#x27;s archetype tells you how it fights; its class, Combat Level, feats, and element make that particular creature different. Normal tier chances are 60% Typical, 30% Elite, and 10% Champion, using Dungeon Level, +1, and +2 respectively. A tier is a Level change, not a secret second set of damage multipliers.</p><p>Shamblers threaten close quarters; Runners close gaps quickly. Deadcrabs are low jumping attackers. Soldiers use ranged fire; Blitzers press aggressively; Snipers punish exposed sight lines.</p><p>BioBlasters threaten with biological attacks. Watchers demand attention to their readable attack tells. Seekers telegraph a committed charge: move out of its path instead of retreating along it.</p><p>Listen, look ahead, and use corners. Killing an enemy does not guarantee a permanently safe floor; wandering populations can replenish. Size, class tint, elemental aura, and aimed information help you decide what to tackle first.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 43</div></article><article class="page" id="enemy-new" data-title="More unwelcome company"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>More unwelcome company</h2><table><tr><td>Climber</td><td>Pink fast-zombie silhouette; climbs to reach you. Watch vertical approaches.</td></tr><tr><td>Nodule</td><td>Stationary gas hazard. Do not stand beside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Flamer</td><td>Red soldier silhouette; warns before a short-range fire attack.</td></tr><tr><td>Big Crab</td><td>Oversized headcrab with a telegraphed fire attack.</td></tr><tr><td>Sentry</td><td>Stationary gun emplacement; break its firing line.</td></tr><tr><td>Razor</td><td>Flying blade with a warned dive. Move off its committed approach.</td></tr><tr><td>Arc Caster</td><td>Marks a target area before its Magic strike. Leave the mark.</td></tr><tr><td>Lurker</td><td>Ceiling ambusher with a venom shot. Look up.</td></tr><tr><td>Beam Sweeper</td><td>Stationary sweeping laser. Interrupt its charge or use cover; gunfire will not cancel an already released beam.</td></tr></table><p>Fire can attempt Immolated; venom can attempt Poisoned. These enemies use the same saves, damage, elements, and progression rules as the rest of the roster.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 44</div></article><article class="page" id="neil" data-title="Neil has the Black Keycard"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Neil has the Black Keycard</h2><div class="boss-art" role="img" aria-label="Neil, Brute, and Gordon the Warden"></div><p>After Yellow Gate, look for Neil: the green-suited bureaucrat clutching a briefcase. Neil flees through the open labyrinth and across connected floors. He does not attack you. He alone carries the Black Keycard.</p><p>Brute is his independently killable antlion-guard escort. It keeps near Neil and reacts when you hit him. Orange warning marks a charge: after a 1.25-second preparation, Brute commits to its direction. Sidestep that line. A wall collision stuns it for two seconds.</p><p>You may defeat the escort first, but Brute is not an invulnerability switch. Neil can be defeated independently. Take the Black Keycard dropped by Neil to progress.</p><p>Neil is fixed at Dungeon Level. Brute is fixed at Dungeon Level +1.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 45</div></article><article class="page" id="gordon" data-title="Gordon the Warden"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Gordon the Warden</h2><div class="boss-art" role="img" aria-label="Neil, Brute, and Gordon the Warden"></div><p>Beyond Black Gate is a two-level arena: a lower court and an upper gallery. Gordon is the heavy man in a pig mask. Entering commits the encounter and closes the back gate.</p><p>An entry or respawn alcove provides protection and one aid allowance per Hero identity per dungeon: up to 25 HP, up to 30 ammunition per owned gun, and one Healing Potion. Repeated entry is not an unlimited supply.</p><p>Above roughly 60% HP, Gordon alternates a three-second cloak with a visible warning before launching four slow homing orbs. Around 60%, he rides his toilet and leaves bombs with three-second fuses. Around 25%, he clears that ordnance and charges with his crowbar.</p><p>If his cloaked phase goes twelve seconds without damage, Gordon reveals himself and pauses attacks for a two-second taunt. Hitting him ends the taunt. Crowbar stagger works once every three seconds against Gordon; gun hit stun keeps its usual rules.</p><p>Fake Gordon Clones join at Dungeon Levels 4, 8, 12 and 16, up to four. Each has one-third of the real Gordon’s maximum HP. They spread around the arena and have no boss health bar. Defeating a clone does not release the Jail Key; defeating the real Gordon ends the encounter.</p><p>The fight does not reset just because a Hero dies. Defeat him, take the Jail Key at the arena center, open the rescue chamber, and reach the damsel—or the cash after Level 20. Gordon&#x27;s death alone never completes the dungeon.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 46</div></article><article class="page" id="fund" data-title="The Debbie Fund"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>The Debbie Fund</h2><div role="img" aria-label="Deborah demonstrates" class="art" style="background-size:300% 200%;background-position:0% 0%"></div><p>The Debbie Fund takes rescue funding very seriously. Its $DEB units are Debbie Coins—&#x27;Debs&#x27;—and its collectibles are Debbie Fund Tokens, or DFTs. These are server-local game records, with no cash value or outside wallet.</p><p>A successful rescue creates a pool of 100 × Dungeon Level Debs. Qualifying Soldier-attributable Hero life losses assign 11% each to the Soldier side, capped at 33% of the pool; Soldier damage contributions determine its allocation.</p><p>The remaining Hero pool is divided half equally and half by damage and effective allied healing, with hostile-loss adjustments. Eligible dead or disconnected participants can retain their claim. Switching to Soldier play forfeits a Hero share.</p><p>Rescue awards increase wallet balance and lifetime rescue earnings. DFT sales increase spendable balance but do not inflate that lifetime rescue score. The staging Heroes of Legend board records the highest dungeon reached, damsels rescued, and cash bags recovered; it is not a count of monster kills.</p><p>At Debbie, choose Fuse Equipment, Sell Equipment, Fuse DFTs, or Sell DFTs. Drag eligible items into the labeled pile, review the value, and confirm. You can also click items to add or remove them. Closing the menu cancels staging without moving anything. Sales award the displayed value in $DEB. Fusion consumes two to eight inputs and returns one legal item worth 85–100% of their combined value and more than any single input; unsupported piles are rejected intact. Equipment fusion returns carried gear; DFT fusion returns a persistent upgraded token. DFT-created gear and free starting weapons cannot be sold or fused. If any fused DFT was recreated this run, the new token remains used for this run. DFT Collection / Recreate retains the free recreation service.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 47</div></article><article class="page" id="tokens" data-title="A little something to keep"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>A little something to keep</h2><div role="img" aria-label="Deborah demonstrates" class="art" style="background-size:300% 200%;background-position:100% 0%"></div><p>DFTs normally mint when a dungeon objective is completed. Combat Level milestones 1, 5, 10, and 20 can each award one token per account on this server. A rare rescue roll also gives each participating Hero a one-in-1,000 chance. Ordinary enemy kills do not mint DFTs. Rescuing Deborah at Level 20 also unlocks Abundance: visit her in staging for one free DFT per Steam account every rolling 24 hours. Reconnecting or restarting a campaign does not reset the timer. The eight-token capacity still applies; a full wallet leaves the gift available until you make room. Recreated equipment retains the usual resale and fusion exclusions.</p><p>Your collection has eight slots. Milestone items waiting for space stay frozen; making room does not reroll them. Tokens persist across ordinary death and campaign restart.</p><p>At the staging Debbie statue, recreate a token&#x27;s frozen item for free once per token per run. The DFT remains in your collection. The same token becomes available to recreate again in the next run.</p><p>You may instead sell a DFT permanently for its displayed Value in Debs. Read the confirmation carefully: selling the token removes it. Wallet viewing is portable; the statue&#x27;s staging, proximity, and role rules still govern its physical services.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 48</div></article><article class="page" id="tips" data-title="Deborah&#x27;s parting advice"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Deborah&#x27;s parting advice</h2><div role="img" aria-label="Deborah demonstrates" class="art" style="background-size:300% 200%;background-position:50% 100%"></div><ol><li>The clock pauses in staging and starts when the first Hero deploys. Every new dungeon gives you thirty minutes.</li><li>Keep a useful spell selected. A bottle in your hand means you are holding a bottle—not casting.</li><li>Move sideways out of committed charges. A longer corridor is not always a safer escape.</li><li>Compare gear drawbacks as carefully as benefits. Keep your permanent feat requirements in mind.</li><li>Use short map checks, read the current objective, and remember the stairs.</li><li>When the Warden falls, finish the job. Jail Key, jail door, Deborah.</li></ol><blockquote>“You&#x27;ve read the book. Now make yourself useful.”<br>— Deborah</blockquote><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 49</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_academic_achievement" data-title="Academic Achievement"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Academic Achievement</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_ACADEMIC_ACHIEVEMENT"><h3>Academic Achievement</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / magic_pool</p><p>Add your positive CHA modifier to your INT modifier when calculating passive Magic regeneration. Regeneration must be permitted.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 50</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_aggressive_personality" data-title="Aggressive Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Aggressive Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_AGGRESSIVE_PERSONALITY"><h3>Aggressive Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / eligible physical attack</p><p>Your next physical attack adds your positive CHA modifier as damage to each target. Cooldown: 1d3 seconds; these timing dice do not explode.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 51</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_aura_burst" data-title="Aura Burst"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Aura Burst</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_AURA_BURST_1"><h3>Aura Burst</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage to enemies within 0 same-floor cells. Sustained drain does not trigger this.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_RADIANCE_2"><h3>Radiance</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Aura Burst</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage to enemies within 1 same-floor cells. Sustained drain does not trigger this. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MAJESTY_3"><h3>Majesty</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Radiance</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage to enemies within 2 same-floor cells. Sustained drain does not trigger this. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 52</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_hitstun_presence" data-title="Unnerving Presence"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Unnerving Presence</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_1"><h3>Unnerving Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 10% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_2"><h3>Dazing Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Unnerving Presence</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 20% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_3"><h3>Overwhelming Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dazing Presence</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 30% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 53</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_intimidation_proc" data-title="Daunting"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Daunting</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_1"><h3>Daunting</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 11% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_2"><h3>Cowing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Daunting</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 22% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_3"><h3>Overawing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Cowing</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 33% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 54</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_menace" data-title="Menacing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Menacing</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_1"><h3>Menacing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Gain +2 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 30% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_2"><h3>Dreadful</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Menacing</p><p>Gain +4 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 25% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_3"><h3>Terrifying</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dreadful</p><p>Gain +4 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 20% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot. Each target’s first Morale save against you per encounter rolls twice and keeps the lower die. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 55</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_nerve" data-title="Iron Nerve"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Iron Nerve</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_NERVE_1"><h3>Iron Nerve</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Gain +2 to Morale saves.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors subject to Morale</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_NERVE_2"><h3>Unbreakable Nerve</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Iron Nerve</p><p>Gain +4 to Morale saves. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors subject to Morale</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 56</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_panic" data-title="Panic Is Contagious"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Panic Is Contagious</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_PANIC"><h3>Panic Is Contagious</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dreadful</p><p>When an enemy fails Morale against you, AI enemies below half HP within 2 connected cells make a Morale check. This cannot cascade again; each target is immune to cascades for 3 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 57</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_personality_aura" data-title="Abrasive Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Abrasive Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_ABRASIVE_PERSONALITY_1"><h3>Abrasive Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Every 3d4 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage to enemies within 0 same-floor cells. Timing dice do not explode.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_NARCISSISM_2"><h3>Narcissism</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Abrasive Personality</p><p>Every 3d4 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage to enemies within 1 same-floor cells. Timing dice do not explode. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MEGALOMANIA_3"><h3>Megalomania</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Narcissism</p><p>Every 3d4 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage to enemies within 2 same-floor cells. Timing dice do not explode. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 58</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_self_actualization" data-title="Self-Actualization"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Self-Actualization</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_SELF_ACTUALIZATION"><h3>Self-Actualization</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / eligible Magic Form</p><p>Add your positive CHA modifier to each target’s magical damage, once after damage multipliers.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 59</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_winning_personality" data-title="Winning Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Winning Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_WINNING_PERSONALITY"><h3>Winning Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17</p><p>Gain +1 intrinsic CHA, up to the ability ceiling. Use the higher of INT or CHA to meet INT feat ability requirements. Other prerequisites still apply.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 60</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_big_guy" data-title="Big Guy"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Big Guy</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_BIG_GUY"><h3>Big Guy</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 and STR 13</p><p>Your body and hurt volume become 30% larger. Gain 15% melee reach and 20% physical push dealt. Your movement hull stays the same. Incompatible with Little Guy.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 61</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_blast_proof" data-title="Blast-Proof"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Blast-Proof</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_BLAST_PROOF"><h3>Blast-Proof</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15</p><p>Stop the first continuation of an incoming exploding damage chain. Keep damage already rolled; other chains continue normally. Cooldown: 2 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 62</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_glow_up" data-title="Glow Up"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Glow Up</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_GLOW_UP"><h3>Glow Up</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires a usable explicit CHA_MOD-derived damage source</p><p>Whenever your own ability adds your positive CHA modifier as damage, also add your positive CON modifier once to that damage event.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an authored CHA_MOD-derived damage source</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 63</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_health_regeneration" data-title="Second Wind"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Second Wind</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_11"><h3>Second Wind</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 11% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_22"><h3>Rapid Recovery</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 / requires Second Wind</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 22% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_33"><h3>Unbroken</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires Rapid Recovery</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 33% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 64</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_not_yet" data-title="Not Yet"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Not Yet</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_NOT_YET"><h3>Not Yet</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15</p><p>Once per dungeon, lethal damage received above 1 HP leaves you at 1 HP and grants 0.5 seconds of damage immunity. Death, respawn and reconnect do not restore this use.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 65</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_poison_proc" data-title="Venomous"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Venomous</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_1"><h3>Venomous</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>Your hit has a 11% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_2"><h3>Toxic</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 / requires Venomous</p><p>Your hit has a 22% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_3"><h3>Virulent</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires Toxic</p><p>Your hit has a 33% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 66</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_steadfast" data-title="Hard to Move"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hard to Move</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_STEADFAST"><h3>Hard to Move</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>Reduce ordinary hit-stun duration and incoming push distance by 25%. Scripted boss effects may ignore this resistance.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 67</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_big_scary" data-title="Big Scary"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Big Scary</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_BIG_SCARY"><h3>Big Scary</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15, STR 13, and CHA 15 / Big Guy; Menacing</p><p>Gain +2 Morale DC when dealing melee damage, physical push or wall-crush damage. This stacks with Menacing.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 68</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_boom_battery" data-title="Boom Battery"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Boom Battery</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_BOOM_BATTERY"><h3>Boom Battery</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 and INT 15 / Capability: exploding_nonmagic_damage_dice</p><p>Every second continuation die in a non-Magic attack restores 1 Magic. Maximum: 5 Magic per attack; never above 100 Magic.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 69</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_crush_panic" data-title="Crash the Party"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Crash the Party</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_CRUSH_PANIC"><h3>Crash the Party</h3><p class="requirement">STR 17 and CHA 17 / Pusher; Dreadful</p><p>Your wall crush forces an eligible target to check Morale, even during its normal recheck cooldown. Once per target every 3 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with physical push</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 70</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_force_of_will" data-title="Force of Will"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Force of Will</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_FORCE_OF_WILL"><h3>Force of Will</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 and WIS 15 / Pusher; Force Multiplier</p><p>Magic that already pushes can trigger Pusher, Shover or Space Hog after Force Multiplier. A successful proc adds 168 units and uses your Pusher wall-slam die. Shared per-target cooldown: 0.5 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, eligible AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 71</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_meteor_strike" data-title="Meteor Strike"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Meteor Strike</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_METEOR_STRIKE"><h3>Meteor Strike</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 and INT 15 / Bash; Cloud Step</p><p>After using Cloud Step, your first Crowbar hit before landing adds one exploding d6 and doubles its Crowbar push. A miss does not consume this strike. Landing resets it.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers with Crowbar-family access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 72</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_tiny_terror" data-title="Tiny Terror"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Tiny Terror</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_TINY_TERROR"><h3>Tiny Terror</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 and CHA 15 / Little Guy; Menacing</p><p>While Little Guy is active, gain +2 Morale DC against enemies within 2 connected cells. This stacks with Menacing.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 73</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_burst_size" data-title="Extra Round"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Extra Round</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_1"><h3>Extra Round</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Add 1 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_2"><h3>Extended Volley</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Extra Round</p><p>Add 2 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_3"><h3>Full Barrage</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Extended Volley</p><p>Add 3 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 74</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_clumsy_proc" data-title="Distracting"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Distracting</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_1"><h3>Distracting</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your hit has a 11% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_2"><h3>Disorienting</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Distracting</p><p>Your hit has a 22% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_3"><h3>Discombobulating</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Disorienting</p><p>Your hit has a 33% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 75</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_exploding_damage_dice" data-title="Perfect Ten"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Perfect Ten</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D10"><h3>Perfect Ten</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your ordinary d10 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 10 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d10 damage rolls</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D8"><h3>Eight Is Enough</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Perfect Ten</p><p>Your ordinary d8 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 8 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d8 damage rolls</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D4"><h3>Fourtunate</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Eight Is Enough</p><p>Your ordinary d4 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 4 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d4 damage rolls</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 76</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_immolate_proc" data-title="Singeing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Singeing</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_1"><h3>Singeing</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your hit has a 11% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_2"><h3>Scorching</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Singeing</p><p>Your hit has a 22% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_3"><h3>Incendiary</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Scorching</p><p>Your hit has a 33% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 77</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_magnum_deadeye" data-title="Deadeye"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Deadeye</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_MAGNUM_DEADEYE"><h3>Deadeye</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Stand perfectly still for 0.5 seconds to empower your next primary attack: double damage with a standard weapon, or triple damage with the .357 Magnum. One attack consumes the aim.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled actors using a standard player weapon</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 78</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_rate_of_fire" data-title="Hair Trigger"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hair Trigger</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_1"><h3>Hair Trigger</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Increase ordinary firearm primary-fire rate by 10%. Reloads, cooling, targeting windups and spacing within bursts stay unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_2"><h3>Rapid Fire</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Hair Trigger</p><p>Increase ordinary firearm primary-fire rate by 20%. Reloads, cooling, targeting windups and spacing within bursts stay unchanged. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_3"><h3>Lead Storm</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Rapid Fire</p><p>Increase ordinary firearm primary-fire rate by 30%. Reloads, cooling, targeting windups and spacing within bursts stay unchanged. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 79</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_reload_cadence" data-title="Quick Reload"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Quick Reload</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD"><h3>Quick Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Reduce ordinary weapon reload time by 20%. This does not shorten SMG cooling or attack windups.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD_2"><h3>Lightning Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Quick Reload</p><p>Reduce ordinary weapon reload time by 40%. This does not shorten SMG cooling or attack windups. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD_3"><h3>Blink Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Lightning Reload</p><p>Reduce ordinary weapon reload time by 60%. This does not shorten SMG cooling or attack windups. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 80</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_shrink" data-title="Little Guy"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Little Guy</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SHRINK"><h3>Little Guy</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Your visible body becomes 30% smaller. Your movement hull, weapon traces and interaction reach stay the same. Incompatible with Big Guy.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 81</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_smg_heat" data-title="Cold Hands"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Cold Hands</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SMG_COLD_HANDS_1"><h3>Cold Hands</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Each SMG round has a 11% chance to add no heat. Overheat threshold: 8. Overheating still locks firing for 2 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers who possess/use the SMG</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_SMG_COLD_HANDS_2"><h3>Ice in the Veins</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Cold Hands</p><p>Each SMG round has a 22% chance to add no heat. Overheat threshold: 10. Overheating still locks firing for 2 seconds. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers who possess/use the SMG</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_SMG_COLD_HANDS_3"><h3>Absolute Zero</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Ice in the Veins</p><p>Each SMG round has a 33% chance to add no heat. Overheat threshold: 12. Overheating still locks firing for 2 seconds. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers who possess/use the SMG</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 82</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_spring_heel" data-title="Spring Heel"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Spring Heel</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SPRING_HEEL"><h3>Spring Heel</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Double the height of voluntary jumps, including Wall Jump and Cloud Step. Ceilings, wall-top barriers and locked routes still block travel.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 83</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_strafe" data-title="Strafer"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Strafer</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_STRAFER_1"><h3>Strafer</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Strafe 11% faster on the ground. Only the sideways component changes on diagonals. The ordinary speed cap still applies.</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_SIDELER_2"><h3>Sideler</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Strafe 22% faster on the ground. Only the sideways component changes on diagonals. The ordinary speed cap still applies. Replaces lower ranks.</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_LATERAL_MOVER_3"><h3>Lateral Mover</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Strafe 33% faster on the ground. Only the sideways component changes on diagonals. The ordinary speed cap still applies. Replaces lower ranks.</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 84</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_wall_jump" data-title="Wall Jump"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Wall Jump</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_WALL_JUMP"><h3>Wall Jump</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Press Jump within 24 units of a vertical wall to jump and kick away. Four uses before landing; no Magic cost. Spring Heel increases the jump height.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 85</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_ammo_regeneration_floor" data-title="Field Supply"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Field Supply</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_AMMO_FLOOR_44"><h3>Field Supply</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13</p><p>Owned regenerative firearm ammunition refills to 44% of family capacity, rounded up. Regeneration timing and capacity stay unchanged; consumables and AR2 secondary ammo are excluded.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with regenerative firearm ammunition</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_AMMO_FLOOR_55"><h3>Deep Reserves</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / requires Field Supply</p><p>Owned regenerative firearm ammunition refills to 55% of family capacity, rounded up. Regeneration timing and capacity stay unchanged; consumables and AR2 secondary ammo are excluded. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with regenerative firearm ammunition</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_AMMO_FLOOR_66"><h3>War Stock</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / requires Deep Reserves</p><p>Owned regenerative firearm ammunition refills to 66% of family capacity, rounded up. Regeneration timing and capacity stay unchanged; consumables and AR2 secondary ammo are excluded. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled he]====]
